      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're struggling to write a character who's truly defeated, and that's a great starting point. To make Elias's story feel honest, you can focus on his inner turmoil and the desperation that comes with it. Instead of trying to find a way out, let him sink deeper into his own despair, and explore the ways in which his hopelessness consumes him. You could even consider having him find ways to temporarily escape his pain, but ultimately, those escapes will only lead to more suffering, making his situation feel even more inescapable.",
